A||N||5||Bandit1973||SideVents on Door Panels...Any suggestions????||||1||
Z||000000||Bandit1973||01-23-2001||08:36 PM||||Okay, I've got an '87 Fiero GT that I'm making into my own creation...I'm installing the PISA "Ferrari 355" styled front fascia, I'm removing the GT spoiler and the next step is to create some kind of vented doors,(kinda like the Ferrari 355).<P>I have access to a plasma-torch, which can cut pencil thin lines through metal like a hot knife through butter. The problem is after I cut huge pieces out of the door skins, I don't know what to do...I want the concave look of the 355 but don't know how to make it work. I was hoping an aftermarket auto company would offer some door-skin replacements, but I have yet to find one. Any help/info would be greatly appreciated. <P>Again, I didn't want an actual "FERRARI" look-a-like, but I just wanted to make my Fiero look a little more Italian. I call it the F-7 project...named after the F-Scale that measures the strength/damage of Tornadoes...F-5/F-6 being the strongest ever accurately reported. Hey, I live in Oklahoma where most folks understand what the F-scale is all too well!!<P>Oh, almost forgot, does anyone know where I can get some cool side-view mirrors?<P>Thanks in advance!!<P>Bandit||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||01-23-2001||09:05 PM||||The door skin is composite on a stock fiero. why are you needing a torch? Are you are planning to alter the door frame work? That's a really bad idea. The door and it's framework are major safety items. altering them is a really bad idea. You can do whatever you want to the exterior skin but don't change the door itself. <P>Also, If you alter the door you will have to alter the entire window system. There is very little room between the window and outer skin. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 01-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||01-23-2001||09:07 PM||||The door skins are plastic not metal, no need for plasma cutters ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||01-23-2001||09:08 PM||||Ya beat me to it Ogre<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FieroGTRacingInc||01-23-2001||11:47 PM||||I would love to do that to mine... I was wondering about the window myself... What about using one of those small scoop's from J.C. Whitney's... Using one of those *BACKWARD'S*... Inside out???   and then do the body work.. Would that work?? They have small ones!!!<P>------------------<BR>1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TOM||01-24-2001||12:33 AM||||What I would do is either make a mold of the door skin, do a clay press then resculpt the door skin and remold it. or cut up a skin and do some sculpt work then mold that.||||reg||1
